<title>FRANCE: EU sells 9,218 tonnes German intervention rye.</title>
<headline>EU sells 9,218 tonnes German intervention rye.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday sold 9,218 tonnes of intervention rye for export, grain officials said.  </p>
<p>The minimum selling price was 88.60 Ecus per tonne, which is worth around $103 per tonne, EU officials said afterwards.</p>
<p>There had been some question marks over the price after reports that it was far lower at around 68 Ecus per tonne.</p>
</text>
